<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates close steady, seen stable.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates close steady, seen stable.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates closed steady on Tuesday on low buying by cash-short textile mills and brokers said they would stay stable on Wednesday.</p>
<p>NIAB-78 was stable at 2,390 rupees per maund (37.32 kg) in the kerb market. Tuesday's Karachi Cotton Association official spot rates in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>				     Tuesday	    December 8</p>
<p>    NIAB-78			2,405		2,405</p>
<p>    K-68			   2,597.50	   2,597.50</p>
<p>    MNH-93			 2,618.50	   2,618.50</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
